  "metadata": {
    "title": "Improved Upper Bounds for Strength-3 Covering Arrays over Six Symbols via Mixed Short and Regular PSL(2, 5) Orbits",
    "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.23877721",
    "publication_date": "2026-11-02",
    "description": "<p>For an integer $t \\ge 1$, the covering array number $\\mathrm{CAN}(t, k, v)$ is the minimum number of rows $N$ in a strength-$t$ covering array $\\mathrm{CA}(N; t, k, v)$ with $k$ columns over $v$ symbols. Identifying $\\{0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5\\}$ with $\\mathbb{P}^1(\\mathbb{F}_5) = \\mathbb{F}_5 \\,{\\cup}\\, \\{\\infty\\}$ under the diagonal action of $G = \\mathrm{PSL}(2, 5)$ ($|G| = 60$), we record that every $G$-orbit on $\\mathbb{P}^1(\\mathbb{F}_5)^k$ ($k \\ge 1$) has size in $\\{6, 30, 60\\}$ (all three occurring for $k \\ge 3$), where each $30$-row orbit is generated canonically by a non-constant binary starter $b \\in \\{0, \\infty\\}^k$ of stabilizer order $2$ in $G$, placing a complement-closed binary pair across the $15$ symbol pairs and projecting bijectively onto $30$-element two-symbol $G$-orbits on every non-constant $3$-column triple. Jointly selecting $1$ constant starter, $5$ binary $\\{0, \\infty\\}^{12}$ starters, and $5$ regular $60$-row starters yields an explicit group-orbit covering array $\\mathrm{CA}(456; 3, 12, 6)$ specified by $11$ vectors, improving $\\mathrm{CAN}(3, 12, 6) \\le 463$ by $7$ rows. Applying conflict-driven tabu row deletion to mixed-$(30, 60)$ $\\mathrm{PSL}(2, 5)$ orbit seeds further establishes $\\mathrm{CAN}(3, 10, 6) \\le 366$ ($&lt; 380$, $-14$ rows) and $\\mathrm{CAN}(3, 11, 6) \\le 418$ ($&lt; 420$, $-2$ rows), with every row in all three arrays verified to be essential. Substituting $\\mathrm{CAN}(3, 10, 6) \\le 366$ into Chateauneuf--Kreher doubling with $\\mathrm{CAN}(2, 10, 6) \\le 48$ then yields $\\mathrm{CAN}(3, 19, 6) \\le \\mathrm{CAN}(3, 20, 6) \\le 606$ ($&lt; 620$, $-14$ rows).</p>",
